WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.900
As Governor, DeSantis

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.469
moves closer to an expected

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:03.636
presidential bid.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:04.304
CNN's case

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:05.305
file has uncovered

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:06.639
some disturbing comments

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.842
by a new DeSantis appointee,

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:09.743
Andrew Kozinski

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:10.510
who is the senior

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.811
editor of K File,

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.246
is joining us now on this.

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:15.482
Andrew, tell us what you found here.

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.149
Yeah, that's right.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:17.784
A history of anti-gay comments

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:19.152
from Ron Perry.

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.920
He was one of those appointed by Ron

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.922
DeSantis to the new board

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.958
governing the special tax district

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.359
that governs Disney.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.360
Now, people

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.897
remember when this group, Disney,

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.699
they spoke out against the don't say

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:33.933
gay bill.

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:36.002
They were effectively punished

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.738
by DeSantis by replacing the old board

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.807
those who had ties to Disney

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:42.776
with this new board.

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:45.512
Now, Perry, he is an Orlando based

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.479
former pastor.

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:48.748
He runs a group called The Gathering

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:51.184
The Gathering had Zoom sessions,

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:53.119
which he later posted on YouTube.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.320
And what we found was

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.955
in those Zoom sessions,

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:58.258
he made a variety of anti-gay comments

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:01.861
There is even this one where he bizarrely

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:03.363
suggests

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:05.999
that water could be turning people gay

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:07.434
because of hormones in it.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:08.701
Let's take a listen to that one.

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:10.804
So

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:14.374
why are there homosexuals today?

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:18.011
There are any number of reasons

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.712
he has ever given.

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.614
Some would say

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:22.515
the increase

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.717
in estrogen in our society is,

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.920
you know, there's estrogen in the water

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.656
from the

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:31.091
from birth control pills.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.192
They can't get it out.

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.227
But the big part

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:35.428
I would suggest to you, based

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.630
upon what it's saying here,

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.632
is the removal of constraint.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:42.368
Well, you remove the constraints

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:46.473
and then evil occurs

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.174
Now, we should first off point out

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:49.909
that there is no evidence

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:52.045
for either of those claims made by him.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.380
We did reach out to

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.615
DeSantis, his administration.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:56.716
We did reach out to Perry.

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:59.085
We didn't hear back from either of them.

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:00.587
You can read those comments

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:01.921
and others from Perry, an article

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.090
we just posted on CNN dot com.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:04.624
All right.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:05.492
We'll be looking for that.

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:07.327
Andrew Kosinski, thank you so much.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:09.429
I want to bring back Kristen Holmes

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:10.463
along with our CNN

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:12.699
national politics reporter. Evan Weekend.

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:13.800
Ever first,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.201
I mean, your reaction

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:17.670
to what Andrew found in this case

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:18.605
file reporting

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:20.373
and do you think this is going to hurt

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.208
Governor DeSantis?

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.176
You know, Brianna,

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:24.410
I don't anticipate

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.712
that there is going to be

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:26.913
any significant

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:29.782
political consequences for the governor.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.485
What we have seen in Florida

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:35.588
is there is a limit to Democratic outrage

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.157
there is a limit. Yes.

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:39.359
We're going to hear Democrats

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:39.993
shake their head

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.528
at this, angry about this,

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:44.097
but there is a limit to what they can do.

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:46.466
Also, in my conversations

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:47.634
with conservatives

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.335
who hold marginalized identities

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:50.637
over the years,

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:52.172
they have suggested that ignorance

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.940
like this rank ignorance like this

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.042
is sort of the cost of doing business

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.677
They agree with Governor DeSantis

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:59.913
on a whole number of policies, taxes,

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:01.347
limited government.

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.483
So is do they

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:04.350
are they going to feel like

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.753
this is great, that this man has referred

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:08.421
to gay folks as deviant,

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.190
shameful, unhealthy,

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.858
suggesting that you become gay

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.893
by drinking tap water?

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:14.761
Probably not.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.396
But I don't see a groundswell

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:17.330
of gay

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.798
conservatives in Florida

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.900
trying to challenge Governor DeSantis

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.368
when they have supported him

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.470
on so many issues in the recent past.

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.940
And you know, Christian DeSantis

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.107
skipping CPAC there.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:30.343
So he gets to avoid one of those

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:31.711
like Nikki Haley moments

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:32.712
that you highlighted

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:34.614
where she's getting kind of heckled

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:35.281
by the pro.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.316
Trump said

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:37.884
he can't avoid the larger

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.419
issue, though, of Trump

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:40.853
and how he navigates

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:41.988
the hold that Trump

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:45.725
clearly has still on part of the GOP

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:48.261
primary.

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:48.995
Well, that's right, Brianna.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.496
And that's been the big question

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.432
is how he's going to walk this fine line.

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:53.433
The thing to remember

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:55.435
is that DeSantis in 2018

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:56.603
not only ran

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:57.537
with the endorsement

00:03:57.537 --> 00:03:59.572
that he sought from Donald Trump,

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.541
he also ran on a MAGA platform.

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:03.276
We all remember that

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.944
ad for Governor in 2018

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:06.012
in which he is reading

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:07.680
the art of the deal to his child.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.015
He's teaching another child

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:10.350
how to build the wall

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.784
and referencing Trump

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:13.286
in that Florida ad nonstop.

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:15.355
So he clearly was trying to appeal

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:15.788
to the base.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:16.522
And I will tell you

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:18.024
that there are a number of people

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:19.525
that I spoke to here

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:20.059
who say that

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.661
they actually liked DeSantis a lot.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.162
Even the people who say they want Trump

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.764
to be president in 20, 24.

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:25.632
So they like to say

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:27.834
is they just don't believe it's his turn.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.502
The question is whether or not

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:30.270
he can continue

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.405
to stave off these insults

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:34.007
from former President Donald Trump.

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:35.642
I mean, for the last several weeks,

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:36.609
we have seen Trump

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:37.710
just go after

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.279
DeSantis audio through social

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:40.013
as well as

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:41.447
in interviews, calling him

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:43.816
disloyal, hitting his COVID policies.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.451
And the list goes on

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:46.019
and on, hitting him

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:48.021
over Social Security and Medicare.

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:50.189
Now, the question again,

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:50.890
whether or not to say

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.692
this can't continue to just blow this off

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:53.493
as noise.

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:54.961
He's not going to hit other Republicans

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.062
or if at some point

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:57.930
he actually decides to take on former

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:58.965
President Trump.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:00.867
And then what does that look like

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:02.835
for this Republican base?

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.003
Do people split?

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.238
Do they go towards Donald Trump?

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:05.638
This is a group

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:06.839
that has been very loyal to him.

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:07.573
But again,

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:08.675
there are people there

00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:10.276
who like Ron DeSantis.

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:12.745
So he has a very fine line here

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:14.547
that he has to navigate

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:16.015
all of these candidates.

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.517
Do and we'll be watching them.

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:19.352
Eva and Kristen, thank you to

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:20.019
both of you.

